{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-geometric-drag","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:mass-geometric-drag","kind":"remark","title":"Mass in the brane tower","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-recursive-brane-tower","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-recursive-brane-tower","tags":["mass","brane-tower","vortex"],"text":"mass-geometric-drag.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:mass-geometric-drag\"></a><p>In the recursive brane tower (<a href=\"#def:recursive-brane-tower\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">recursive brane tower</a>), mass is not an intrinsic property of a point-particle. Instead, it measures the resistance encountered by a stable vortex propagating through the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-jet bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^1 \\mathcal{S}_n</code> (<a href=\"#prop:jet-prolongation\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">jet prolongation</a>). The substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> (<a href=\"#def:substrate-parameter\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter\">substrate parameter</a>) varies from fibre to fibre. Translating the vortex along the base therefore forces a corresponding variation of the Frobenius--Hopf structure on each fibre. The mass quantifies this variation.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-geometric-drag.md","heading":"Remark","number":"11.1.9","page":"b/rem-mass-geometric-drag","qa":{"counts":{"pass":61,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":23,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
